# Local dev secrets for @aec/web (SSR Worker). Copy to `.dev.vars` and fill in.
# `.dev.vars` is git-ignored at the repo root. For deployed Workers, push
# secrets via: wrangler secret put <KEY> --env <preview|production>

ENV=preview

# ─── Observability (ADR 0024) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing to set. The browser and Worker planes both run on PostHog, which
# authenticates with the publishable `phc_` POSTHOG_PROJECT_KEY — a committed
# per-env `vars` entry in wrangler.jsonc, not a secret (AECI-640). The four
# DD_* Datadog credentials were deleted in AECI-651; if you have them in a
# local `.dev.vars`, drop them.

# ─── Cache-tag purge (AECI-56) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# ADMIN_PURGE_TOKEN: bearer the caller of POST /admin/purge must present.
#   Locally pick anything (e.g. `dev-admin-token`). In deployed envs push via
#   `wrangler secret put ADMIN_PURGE_TOKEN --env <preview|production>`.
# /admin/purge invalidates natively via ctx.cache.purge() (WC-6) — it no longer
# reads a Cloudflare API token (CF_PURGE_API_TOKEN was retired in WC-10).
# Optional locally — the endpoint 401s until the token is set. Don't commit real values.
ADMIN_PURGE_TOKEN=

# ─── Algolia search (AECI-134) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# ALGOLIA_APP_ID + ALGOLIA_SEARCH_KEY are explicitly client-exposed: the SSR
# Worker renders them into the HTML (window.__AECI_ALGOLIA__) so InstantSearch
# (3.9) can pick them up at hydration. The SEARCH key is query-only and scoped
# to this env's three indexes. Both no-op when empty (no script injected), so
# dev boots cleanly without an Algolia account.
# The Algolia ADMIN/management key is NEVER set on the web Worker — it would
# reach the browser. It lives only on the API Worker (apps/api/.dev.vars.example).
# Provision real per-env values with `node scripts/algolia/provision.mjs` and
# push them with `wrangler secret put ALGOLIA_APP_ID/ALGOLIA_SEARCH_KEY --env <env>`.
ALGOLIA_APP_ID=
ALGOLIA_SEARCH_KEY=

# ─── Supabase auth (AECI-193 / Phase 5) ──────────────────────────────────────
# SUPABASE_URL + SUPABASE_ANON_KEY are read by the SSR Worker at runtime: they
# feed `createSupabaseServerClient` (src/server/auth/supabase-server-client.ts),
# the cookie-session factory behind /auth/*. The anon (publishable) key is not
# truly secret — it's stored as a secret only to keep values out of git (same
# convention as ALGOLIA_SEARCH_KEY). Both empty → auth surfaces return 503
# `auth_not_configured` and everything else works. For local dev use the single
# shared auth project (ADR 0017 — https://ktuhnlypztujpsseujzx.supabase.co);
# fetch the key with `supabase projects api-keys --project-ref ktuhnlypztujpsseujzx`.
# The service-role key is NEVER set on any Worker (AUTH_AND_RLS.md §3).
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Test-user credentials. NEVER a Worker binding; the Worker does not read these.
# Two consumers, both off the same recipe (capture a real `@supabase/ssr` session):
#   1. apps/web/scripts/mint-dev-session.mjs — mints a session cookie / bearer for
#      the /auth/whoami 200-path smoke (manual).
#   2. apps/web/e2e/authed-console.spec.ts (AECI-235) — read via playwright.config.ts
#      to console-check the auth-gated Phase 5 pages (/account, /admin, /admin/reviews,
#      /products/:slug/review).
# For (2) the user must be the ADMIN test@thewbsproject.com, AND its `role='admin'`
# D1 profile (apps/api/seed/auth-fixtures.sql, keyed to that account's Supabase user
# id) must be seeded — `dev:bound` → `db:seed:local` does this automatically. A valid
# non-admin user makes the /admin* cases FAIL (not skip); absent creds → they skip.
# See docs/environments.md → "Local dev: Supabase auth (Phase 5)".
SUPABASE_TEST_USER_EMAIL=
SUPABASE_TEST_USER_PASSWORD=

# ─── PostHog (AECI-239 / Phase 7.4; renamed + demoted AECI-640) ──────────────
# POSTHOG_PROJECT_KEY is the `phc_` project API key. It is PUBLISHABLE — the SSR
# Worker inlines it into the HTML (window.__AECI_POSTHOG__) on every page, so it
# is not a secret and cannot be one. On deployed tiers it is a committed per-env
# `vars` entry in wrangler.jsonc, NOT a pushed secret; it appears here only
# because local dev has no wrangler env block to inherit from.
#
# POSTHOG_HOST is the INGEST host and defaults to https://us.i.posthog.com when
# empty. Note `us.posthog.com` (no `.i`) is the MANAGEMENT API — swapping them
# produces a confusing 404. The static CSP connect-src is pinned to the US ingest
# + assets hosts, so a non-US host needs a matching CSP change
# (src/server/seo-headers.ts).
#
# Leaving POSTHOG_PROJECT_KEY empty is the recommended local default: no script
# is injected, the browser layer no-ops, and the Worker's own telemetry no-ops
# too, so dev boots cleanly and your local traffic never lands in a shared
# project. Fill it with the non-prod key (project `aec-integrations-dev`, 525793)
# only when you are deliberately verifying the pipes.
POSTHOG_PROJECT_KEY=
POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# ─── IndexNow verification key (AECI-236 / §20.2) ─────────────────────────────
# The SSR Worker serves `{INDEXNOW_KEY}.txt` at the site root so search engines
# can verify host ownership before honoring the IndexNow submissions the API
# Worker sends on promote. Read at runtime; set as a CI-pushed Wrangler secret:
#   wrangler secret put INDEXNOW_KEY --env production
# Must MATCH the API Worker's INDEXNOW_KEY. 8–128 chars [A-Za-z0-9-]. Absent →
# the key file 404s (graceful no-op) — the expected state until public launch,
# when it is provisioned alongside ALLOW_INDEXING="true".
INDEXNOW_KEY=
